# Worktree status footer

Copyright (c) 2026 Devrecated.

When this window’s folder is a **linked git worktree** (`.git` is a file, not a directory), end **every** reply with this block, values filled in:

```text
- worktree: <directory>
- branch: <name>
- commits: <origin/master..HEAD onelines or (none)>
- created: <iso date>
- pushed: <true|false>
- checkout: cursor --reuse-window <directory>
```

`pushed` is `true` only if an upstream exists and HEAD is not ahead.

A `stop` hook may send one follow-up if you omit the block. Append it and stop. Do not start new work.

Primary checkout: omit the block.

To silence the hook: [hookignore](hookignore.mdc) (`worktree-status`).
